{"name":"Anarchist","hex":"#db304a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"anarchist","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who believes in or advocates the absence of hierarchy and authority in most forms (compare anarchism), especially one who works toward the realization of such.","One who disregards laws and social norms as a form of rebellion against authority."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to anarchism or to anarchists; anarchistic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anarchist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anarchism","blocks":[{"text":"Anarchism is a far-left political philosophy and movement that seeks to abolish all institutions that perpetuate authority, coercion, or hierarchy, primarily targeting the state, capitalism, and organised religion. Anarchism advocates for the replacement of these hierarchical social structures with stateless societies consisting of horizontal networks of voluntary associations that operate based on the principles of free association and reciprocity. Anarchism is described as being part of the libertarian wing of the socialist movement, broadly known as libertarian socialism."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anarchism","wikidata":"Q6199"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Portrait_Pierre-Joseph_Proudhon_by_Nadar_%E2%80%93_BNF.jpg/500px-Portrait_Pierre-Joseph_Proudhon_by_Nadar_%E2%80%93_BNF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Portrait_Pierre-Joseph_Proudhon_by_Nadar_%E2%80%93_BNF.jpg/1280px-Portrait_Pierre-Joseph_Proudhon_by_Nadar_%E2%80%93_BNF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Portrait_Pierre-Joseph_Proudhon_by_Nadar_%E2%80%93_BNF.jpg/500px-Portrait_Pierre-Joseph_Proudhon_by_Nadar_%E2%80%93_BNF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe